fields.description:
Operation selector. Chooses the manual read, page-program or erase operation sent to the serial engine.

Usage: Software programs this field before asserting go.

Values:
0x0 Read operation;
0x1 Program operation;
0x2 Erase operation;
0x3 Reserved encoding.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Serial lane mode value. The low two bits select standard SPI, dual-lane or quad-lane data phases.

Usage: Software configures lane mode before a manual transfer; XIP mode selection is derived from this field.

Values:
0x0 Standard SPI, one lane;
0x1 Dual SPI, two lanes;
0x2 Quad SPI, four lanes;
0x3 Reserved encoding.

Unit: none.

Limits: Only bits 1 through 0 affect lane selection; other bits are stored but ignored.
